{
  "_README": [
    "NIGERIAN NAME CORPUS — used to build the known-negative evaluation set.",
    "",
    "OWNER: expand freely. These are common given names and surnames across the",
    "three largest Nigerian language groups. They are combined",
    "combinatorially by src/eval/corpus.ts to synthesise the 5,000 'ordinary",
    "customer' names that must NOT match any sanctions entry.",
    "",
    "IMPORTANT: these are population-typical names, deliberately NOT taken from",
    "any watchlist. The eval cross-checks every generated name against the",
    "ingested OFAC list and discards any genuine collision before measuring, so",
    "adding a name that happens to appear on a list will not silently corrupt",
    "the false-positive number.",
    "",
    "The point of this file is that the false-positive measurement is made",
    "against realistic African names rather than the Anglo-European test data",
    "screening vendors tune on. That difference IS the headline result."
  ],
